# Firmware upload — OTA first

When the user needs to flash c3-mini-bot WiFi firmware, **always give the OTA command**:

```bash
cd c3-mini-bot
pio run -e c3_mini_wifi_ota -t upload
```

- Hostname: `c3-bot1.local` (set `upload_port` + `BOT_OTA_HOSTNAME` in `platformio_private.ini` `[ota]` section)
- Bot must be on WiFi with OTA-capable firmware already running
- First-ever flash: one USB `c3_mini_wifi_ota` upload, then OTA only

Do not suggest USB unless user explicitly asks.

## Safety — bot must be stopped

**Never OTA while the bot is moving.** Stop `fleet-brain`, zero `/bot1/cmd_vel`, confirm stationary, or get Cain's OK. See `ota-safety.mdc`.

## Other envs

| Env | Use |
|-----|-----|
| `c3_mini_wifi_ota` | **Default** — fleet + OTA |
| `c3_mini_wifi` | USB only (no OTA in firmware) |
| `c3_bench` | USB bench test |
| `c3_autonomous` | USB standalone wander |
